 The separate engine-only completion path remains outside this form contract.
+
+### Bounded archived start-form contract
+
+`FormService.getFormData(null, processDefinitionId)` reads the ordinary start
+form in that exact definition deployment. `ProcessInstanceService.startProcessInstance`
+accepts `values` keyed by declared editable field ID, separately from raw
+`variables`. Nonempty archived start forms require validated values; unknown,
+read-only/unsupported fields, required omissions, invalid types and placeholder
+or unknown dropdown options refuse before any Flowable start command. A supplied
+`formId` must resolve to the start event's form in the same deployment. Raw
+variable injection is refused for these forms; caller `variables.initiator` is
+ignored and the authenticated JWT or legacy Insight principal supplies identity.
+Empty FormApp start forms and processes without archive mappings retain their
+existing variable-only start behavior. This is principal validation, not a new
+process-specific group/tenant ACL policy.
+
+The bounded mapping preserves field IDs and validated payload types
+(text/date strings and table row lists). Inline dropdown submissions become the
+schema option ID plus `<field>_LABEL`, taking the label from the deployed options
+rather than trusting a submitted name. Explicit nulls remain explicit clears;
+missing optional fields stay absent. Generic field bindings, execution mappings,
+REST option loading, upload/content binding and legacy JavaScript are unsupported.
+Task submission keeps its existing payload contract.
+
+`ArchivedStartFormScenarioTest` uses real Flowable and isolated PostgreSQL
+schemas with persisted Insight users, notification outbox and content entity
+mappings. Its carrier BPMN is explicitly synthetic (ordinary start → assigned
+wait → end); it does not modify or execute a customer BPMN archive. Exact archived
+form bytes are pinned: PPStart-3 SHA-256
+`79842ee07ace272215263d8fbe627b8be556488e90cb07bc8879871b53cae2cf`
+and AnalystStart-13 SHA-256
+`246bead0482ed82b3ac00cf4265985cbb4ad06a28bb5ca0fdc59f89f44fa4197`.
+The existing archive provenance and sanitization receipts remain authoritative.
+PPStart uses aliases 318/source 3; AnalystStart uses 297/source 13. FormApp's
+MDCR-23 start resource has no fields; MDCR's process has no start form.
+
+These are actual start-form receipts **on isolated carriers only**: JWT/legacy
+identity, transport JSON roundtrip, declared values and canonical labels,
+persisted runtime/history, refusal with no process/task/history/outbox/content
+rows and deployment-local version selection. They do not certify an ETC renderer,
+customer notifications or downstream customer journeys. Feedback remains
+published-but-not-runnable and Analysis publication remains refused by
+`CustomerArchivePublicationTest`. Both Safran seed manifests declare
+`optionSources: []`; no persisted dynamic-option parity is claimed. A reviewed,
+source-backed workflow migration and option-source mapping remain **open
+prerequisites for actual customer journey coverage**. No Administration/PDC-005
+policy is inferred.
 The preflight inventory continues to report static publication gaps; it is not a
 behavioral certification. Follow the repository quality bar (Unit tests and
 Build locally, then the exact-head Jenkins/Sonar PR gates).
